WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:09.260
Famously start with e

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:10.240
raise to Pi with an i

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:11.460
then we're taught by a lot

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:12.340
that you've got

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:13.120
minus 1

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:14.140
Can we glean what it means?

00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:15.800
For such words are absurd

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:16.820
How to treat the repeat of a feat

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:18.160
Pi I times

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:19.880
This is bound to confound

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:20.820
'til your mind redefines

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:22.060
these amounts one can't count

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:23.720
which surmount our friend e.

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:25.000
Numbers act as abstract

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:26.400
functions which slide the rich

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.000
2d space in its space with a grace

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:28.880
when they sum.

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:30.640
Multiplied, they don't slide,

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:31.600
acting a second way

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:33.540
They rotate, and dilate, but keep straight

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:34.320
that same plane.

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:35.760
Now that we write as e

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:36.840
to the x won't perplex

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:37.780
when you know it's for show

00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:39.040
that 'x' goes up and right.

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:40.200
It does not, as you thought,

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:41.420
repeat e product e.

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:43.360
It functions with gumption on functions

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:44.080
we've now seen.

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:45.800
It turns slides side to side

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:47.100
into growths and shrinks both.

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:48.440
Up and downs come around

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:49.900
as turns round which is key!

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:51.180
This is why Pi times i,

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:52.720
which slides north is brought forth

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:53.840
and returned, we have learned,

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:54.920
as a turn halfway round.

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:56.880
Minus one, matched by none.

00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:58.420
Turns this way hence we're done.

